WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.360
How many of you have got it?

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:28.800
Okay, I will give one copy here
for your library —

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.000
you can all share it.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.840
At the outset, I must confess
that the title Gita Enlightened

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.120
may be a little misleading.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:45.040
I by no means profess to
enlighten the Gita,

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:51.595
but I humbly say that it has
been written through enlightened eyes —

00:00:51.595 --> 00:01:05.600
eyes that have been enlightened
by Her Holiness Shri Mataji Nirmala Devi.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:25.600
So, what happened was, in the
year '81, Shri Mataji was going

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:35.200
to a resort in Coimbatore for
a month, and just by the way

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.640
she said, "You want to come?"

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:39.200
Of course — any way I can
be with Shri Mataji.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:45.200
So we were there in Coimbatore,
just the two of us and nobody else.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:53.040
I had been talking about the Gita
— having read over a hundred books

00:01:53.040 --> 00:02:04.080
on it and heard several discourses
by many self-proclaimed gurus

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:13.200
and so-called eminent intellectuals —
and I had only gotten more confused.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:21.520
It was at this turning point in
my life that destiny brought me

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:24.320
to the feet of Her Holiness.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:29.840
And when I questioned her on
these subtle points of the Gita,

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:36.560
its apparent contradictions,
its juxtapositions,

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:43.040
she so simply and with such
profound wisdom threw immense

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:50.960
light on them that I recognized
what a storehouse of knowledge she is.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:53.520
I had been writing things about
the Gita, and she said,

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:58.080
"Okay, now forget everything
that you have read or written

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:00.240
about the Gita."

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:06.160
And she started from the very
beginning — and the beginning

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:08.960
was completely different
from everything else.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:15.200
She said, "It's all about Draupadi.
It's all about chastity.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.840
It's all about the Ganesh Tatva."

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:23.840
The first and foremost thing we
have to understand is that

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:32.400
Shri Krishna is a divine incarnation,
and He came at a time

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:43.040
when we needed to understand
the essence of dharma.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:49.200
For example, I have been quite
surprised by the way people

00:03:49.200 --> 00:04:00.320
explain Him. As far as Ahimsa
is concerned, they have preached

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:03.920
it to such an extent that we
have to look after all the

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:06.800
mosquitoes of Delhi.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:14.240
Such absurd things people have
deduced from what Krishna

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:24.400
tried to emphasize in the Shri Gita.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:32.160
And this itself explained to me
what Lord Krishna meant when

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:36.320
Arjuna asked Him which of the
two paths is greater —

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:40.640
the path of Jnana or the path
of Bhakti.

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:46.880
Lord Krishna, although He said
that both lead to the same goal,

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:51.040
in the end says, "The one who
loves Me is dear to Me."

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:55.600
Now, this may have escaped the
attention of many readers —

00:04:55.600 --> 00:05:01.440
that having said both paths lead
to the same goal, why does

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:04.400
He then say this?

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:09.360
Because in this very verse
lies the whole secret:

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:16.000
that the knowledge we seek
through our intellect is limited.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:19.760
It is our limited intelligence,
because it is the intelligence

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:24.000
of the individual and therefore
limited by his ego.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:30.320
So it was the Ganesh Tatva that
is the basis of everything,

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:41.640
and when that is insulted,
then the Shakti —

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:46.480
the intervention of the Divine —
takes place.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:51.760
One example: at the time of the
war, Karna — the great,

00:05:51.760 --> 00:06:00.080
generous man, very well known
for his virtues —

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:06.400
got caught up in a wheel of
his chariot and could not

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.240
get his leg out.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:23.440
When Arjuna faced him and
raised his Gandiva, Karna

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:34.400
challenged him, saying,
"A chivalrous person,

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:49.920
a fellow warrior — in dharma,
when I have no weapons on me,

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:53.000
you cannot kill me with
your weapons."

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:58.320
At that moment, Shri Krishna
pointed at him and said,

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:05.680
"Kill him. Where were his
warrior virtues when

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:09.680
Draupadi was insulted?

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:15.120
Draupadi's insult was the
greatest sin that was committed,

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:20.000
and what was he doing at
that time?"

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:29.760
And Arjuna killed Karna.
This is dharma.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:41.200
He is called Leeladhara — the
one for whom the whole world

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:50.400
is a play. And that's why He
says, "They are already killed."

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:54.480
That doesn't mean you start
killing people, becoming violent,

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:56.240
because you don't agree
with someone.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:08:04.480
Only Shri Krishna can say
whom to kill.

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:10.320
You have to be a realized soul
to understand why Shri Krishna

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:15.440
had to ask Arjuna to kill,
and why the Goddess had to

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:22.000
kill so many demons.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:28.040
But the idea today is that we
should try to be sympathetic

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:34.000
even towards demons, towards
the devils who are spreading

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:44.000
Asurividya everywhere — that
we should be sympathetic

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.960
with all people, that there
is good in everyone.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:53.680
That's not Krishna's message.
He showed His love by killing

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:55.680
the demons.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:09:01.040
So it's all about the chastity
of Draupadi being challenged

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:06.320
by Duryodhana. That's where
it started.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:09.840
So the whole angle was completely
different — nobody had ever

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:17.360
given this interpretation of
the Gita before.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:22.080
It started with Ganesha, and
then it went from one chakra

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:27.920
to another, to the Vishuddhi,
and then beyond the Vishuddhi.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:36.956
What surprised me most about
what Shri Krishna said —

00:09:36.956 --> 00:09:39.600
and what she explained — was this:
"But they are already dead."

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:42.400
Shri Krishna said, "I have
already killed them.

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:45.360
What are you doing, Arjuna?
You do nothing.

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:47.600
You think you are going to
kill them? I have already killed them."

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:50.160
So I said, "But how are they
dead? They are alive,

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:51.520
they are on the battlefield."

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:59.040
She said, "They are dead
because their spirit has been betrayed."

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:11.680
And the war started. Arjuna
actually became nervous,

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:17.200
I would say, and said, "I would
not like to fight my own

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:21.520
kith and kin, and my gurus."

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:28.880
So Shri Krishna says, "They
are already dead. They are killed.

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:35.920
These are already dead people —
their eyes are not open.

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:40.880
Whom are you going to kill here?
You just have to remove

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:47.280
some people from this earth
to establish dharma."

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:50.800
Now, the idea of dharma,
according to us, is some sort

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:56.240
of Hinduism, or Islam, or
some other "-ism." It is not.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:04.400
In a human being — just as
carbon has four valencies —

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:05.760
dharma has ten valencies.

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:11.760
And when a person falls from
these, he loses his powers

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:14.720
as a human being.

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:17.920
When you betray your spirit,
you are dead, because you

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:19.680
have no use to evolution —

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:23.680
you have gone out of evolution,
like the dinosaurs who went

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:26.960
out of evolution.

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:31.600
So whether your physical body
is there or not makes no

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:37.440
difference to the Divine.

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:46.240
That was the very deep
essence of the Gita.

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:51.920
So then she said, "All right —
even in Sahaja Yoga,

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:53.920
nobody is going to tell
you, do this."

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:58.320
So — you've done this, why did
you wear jeans to a puja,

00:11:58.320 --> 00:11:59.680
and so forth?

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:02.080
You have a free hand,
do what you want.

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:06.720
But if you go against the
spirit, you will lose your vibrations.

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:13.120
You are the loser.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:20.080
So I said, but Arjuna had this
vision of Shri Krishna —

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:24.320
the Virata — yet he still had
doubts in his mind,

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:28.480
he was still asking questions.

00:12:29.840 --> 00:12:37.280
If you see God but you don't
have the recognition,

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:41.360
you will miss it.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:45.760
So the point, she says, is not
to see God — I mean,

00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:48.000
the point is not to have
a vision of God.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:53.440
"People see me every day,"
she said, "but they don't believe in me.

00:12:53.440 --> 00:13:01.200
You have to discover your own
kundalini, your own divinity.

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:04.160
Then you will know who I am."

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:08.960
Unless and until you experience
your own spirit, how can

00:13:08.960 --> 00:13:11.280
you experience God?

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:18.240
So the point was not to see
the Virata — the point was

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:30.320
to experience your own spirit.
That is the thing.

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:35.520
You think you know God,
but you don't know God.

00:13:35.520 --> 00:13:38.960
You have a concept of God —
that God is this, God is that —

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:45.280
you make an idol, you make
a murti, but God is not that.

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:51.520
That is your concept of God,
and you may worship that concept,

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:54.800
but that is not the reality.

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:58.160
That doesn't mean you're
following God.

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:06.240
Even in Greek mythology, they
humanized their gods,

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:08.720
and then those gods fight
with each other,

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:14.152
each claiming their god is
superior to the other's.

00:14:14.152 --> 00:14:17.840
But the question isn't whose
God is superior.

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:23.840
The question isn't whether
God is on your side.

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:27.200
The question is: are you
on God's side?

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:30.160
And how will you know you
are on God's side?

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:33.520
All these fanatics, all these
terrorists, all these fundamentalists —

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:36.160
they say they are doing
God's work.

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:37.600
But how do you know you're
doing God's work?

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:42.640
You're only pampering your own
ego, only following your own ego.

00:14:42.640 --> 00:14:46.480
You'll only know when you know
yourself, when you know your own spirit.

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:51.200
And the person who knows his
own spirit can never be a fanatic,

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:56.320
can never be a fundamentalist —
because the spirit is the same

00:14:56.320 --> 00:15:00.320
in everyone, and if you have
felt your own spirit,

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:06.880
you will not hurt that same
spirit in another person.

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:12.480
We are different bodies,
but the spirit is the same.

00:15:12.480 --> 00:15:20.960
That is what she explained
is the essence of the Gita.

00:15:20.960 --> 00:15:30.320
So Arjuna is blinded by his
attachment to his relationships

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:39.600
in the enemy ranks — his teachers,
Dronacharya, Bhishma Pitamaha,

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:40.880
and all that.

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:47.040
He's not able to come out of
that; he doesn't want to hurt them.

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:48.960
He says, "How can I kill them?
They are my this,

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:55.520
they are my that," all that.
This is emotional attachment.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:16:00.960
So we can say that through
the right side, you get

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:05.040
attachment to the ego, when
you get fixed ideas,

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:10.160
or you get attached to an
ideology — "this is communism,

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:13.200
this is democracy, this is that."

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:19.520
But there's also the attachment
to your super-ego —

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:23.200
"this is my relation, this is
this, this is that."

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:28.560
Both have to be overcome.
We have to get detached from both.

00:16:30.560 --> 00:16:35.440
But that doesn't mean you
become a dry personality.

00:16:35.440 --> 00:16:40.000
You enjoy everybody, but you're
not attached to anybody —

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:42.080
that is the thing.

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:46.800
Earlier, you were very curious
about everybody —

00:16:46.800 --> 00:16:52.320
"What is he doing? What is that?" —
and now you're only curious about God.

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:55.520
So all other curiosities are gone.

00:16:55.520 --> 00:17:01.600
When you become attached to
the curiosity of God,

00:17:02.320 --> 00:17:06.560
you get detached from all
other curiosities.

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:10.560
Nothing else matters. "Oh, he's
doing this — let him do it.

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:14.400
He's this — so what?
He's a minister — so what?"

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:20.880
Nothing, nothing, nothing.
That's like that bhajan

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:25.600
of Shankaracharya — tadakim,
tadakim — "this, not this."

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:36.240
It's there. You're not blind
to it, but you're not attached to it.

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:44.480
So that was the Gita. She said,
"Call it Gita Enlightened" —

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:50.000
that this Gita, which has been
misunderstood, which has been

00:17:50.000 --> 00:18:01.360
parroted without self-realization,
has now become enlightened.

00:18:01.360 --> 00:18:02.400
Now you can understand.

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:05.360
Only a Sahaja Yogi can
understand the message

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:16.160
of Shri Krishna. But then she
added that Shri Krishna

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:25.680
gave realization to only
one person, to Arjuna.

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:38.000
Arjuna saw Him as a very huge,
big personality,

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:44.080
and saw in Him all human beings
and all creation moving about,

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:48.480
and he couldn't bear it anymore —
he said, "I don't want to see it again."

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:54.960
Shri Krishna spoke the Gita
only to Arjuna,

00:18:54.960 --> 00:19:00.960
only to one person — He didn't
tell it to even a second person,

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:03.913
because He was born six
thousand years ago,

00:19:03.913 --> 00:19:06.800
and at that time people's
maturity was so low

00:19:06.800 --> 00:19:13.840
that He did not tell it to
anybody else but Arjuna.

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:19.040
This was heard by another
person who wrote it down —

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:22.400
Vyasa is the poet who
wrote about it.

00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:27.760
But now the time has come — the
"blossom time," as she calls it —

00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:32.240
when thousands can give
realization, en masse.

00:19:32.240 --> 00:19:36.720
Giving one person realization
doesn't change anything.

00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:40.560
If you want to change the
world, it has to happen

00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:45.680
en masse, all over the world.

00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:54.640
And that is what Sahaja Yoga
is doing, and it has made a difference.

00:19:54.640 --> 00:20:03.040
It has brought much greater
awareness into human consciousness.

00:20:03.040 --> 00:20:09.520
A lot of things that people
were earlier not sensitive to,

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:13.440
now they are.

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:18.160
This is the change that has
taken place, and things are changing —

00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:20.240
things are moving very fast.

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:24.400
People are getting exposed
very fast; negativity is

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:28.160
getting exposed very fast.

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:31.680
Earlier it was not like that.

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:36.880
So it's not that negativity
isn't there — it is there,

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:40.320
but it's getting exposed.

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:44.000
So many scandals are
getting exposed.

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:46.800
All these things which are
against the Muladhara,

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:49.760
which have been going on in
social media —

00:20:49.760 --> 00:20:52.400
now countries are banning them.

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:57.333
They say this is bad for young
people, because there's

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:03.440
a certain level of awareness now.

00:21:03.440 --> 00:21:10.320
Earlier, people were oblivious
of it. So all this is now coming.

00:21:13.360 --> 00:21:17.120
Sahaja Yoga is bringing this
global transformation,

00:21:17.120 --> 00:21:20.636
and that is what we call the
power of Shri Kalki —

00:21:20.636 --> 00:21:25.360
the power of Shri Kalki is your
power, working collectively.

00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:33.040
It is not a power of destruction;
it is a power of transformation.

00:21:35.280 --> 00:21:41.520
A great movement of evolution
is taking place through all

00:21:41.520 --> 00:21:49.360
of you, each one of you —
wherever you are,

00:21:49.360 --> 00:21:57.120
things are getting transformed.
You will not even know it.

00:21:57.120 --> 00:22:02.320
But your presence... At a
mundane level, I'll say

00:22:02.320 --> 00:22:06.800
that if you go into an office,
people notice you.

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:09.920
They want to sit next to you,
they want to talk to you,

00:22:09.920 --> 00:22:13.280
because they feel a kind of
relaxation when they are

00:22:13.280 --> 00:22:16.240
talking to you.

00:22:16.240 --> 00:22:18.320
Then they ask you, "What is it
that you are doing?

00:22:18.320 --> 00:22:22.240
You are always so calm, you
are always so relaxed,

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:31.120
and we feel very happy in
your presence." It's felt like that.

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:36.160
But at a global level, it is
working through all the

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:40.480
governments, through all the
heads of government,

00:22:40.480 --> 00:22:44.080
and very fast — even with wars.

00:22:44.080 --> 00:22:49.440
People are now understanding
the futility of war.

00:22:49.440 --> 00:22:54.560
Earlier, the powerful countries
thought, "We are the most

00:22:54.560 --> 00:22:57.920
powerful, we can do
anything we want."

00:22:57.920 --> 00:23:05.600
War is not the way.
War is not the way to win —

00:23:05.600 --> 00:23:08.080
they have realized that.

00:23:08.080 --> 00:23:13.600
They used to say that power
flows through the barrel of a gun.

00:23:13.600 --> 00:23:19.360
Not anymore. It flows through
your kundalini, through your

00:23:19.360 --> 00:23:24.560
love, through self-realization.

00:23:24.560 --> 00:23:32.800
This is the future of humanity,
and this will save humanity.

00:23:32.800 --> 00:23:39.360
God did not create this world
to be destroyed.

00:23:39.360 --> 00:23:45.120
Shri Krishna played holy
to spread joy —

00:23:45.120 --> 00:23:54.560
to be joyous. That is the
message of the Gita. Okay?

00:23:54.560 --> 00:24:02.881
Jai Shri Mataji. Jai Shri Mataji.

